{"role":"assistant","content":"Now I have a complete picture of the commit. Let me delegate the review to subagents.","reasoning_content":"I now have a good understanding of the commit. This is a Godot game project with scene files (.tscn) and a tileset resource. The commit \"Parallaxing halfway done\" adds parallax scrolling backgrounds to multiple level scenes. Let me now delegate this to subreviewers.I'll invoke the relevant subreviewer agents. Since this is a code review involving scene files, scripts, and game assets, I should use the appropriate reviewers.","tool_calls":[{"id":"g9hq68yEpEKFSXoMLVnJTk7NcU307fK7","type":"function","function":{"name":"task","arguments":"{\"description\":\"Review Godot scene parallax changes\",\"agent\":\"subreviewer\",\"prompt\":\"Review commit 215cf7c (hash: 215cf7ca6a3a3f67cffec858bec8fcff7ff15b0f) titled \\\"Parallaxing halfway done\\\". This is a Godot game project with scene files (.tscn) and a tileset resource (.tres).\\n\\nThe commit modifies:\\n- levels/00_forest/01.tscn - Added parallax scrolling layers (BackgroudSky, OtherTreeFar, OtherTreeClose, BackgroundTreesFartherAway, BackgroundTreesClose, BackgroundProps) with varying scroll_scales (0, 0.2, 0.3, 0.4, 0.6, 0.8), plus a Fog Sprite2D with gradient texture. Also updated LevelBounds position/height.\\n- levels/00_forest/02.tscn - Similar parallax additions, added multiple level transitions, added Fog.\\n- levels/00_forest/03.tscn - Similar parallax additions, added Fog.\\n- levels/level.tscn - NEW FILE: A template/prototype level with parallax layers and Fog.\\n- levels/tilesets/forgotten_forest.tres - Added a TileMapPattern sub_resource.\\n- levels/tutorial/tutorial.tscn - Added a new TutorialNode and modified existing tutorial text.\\n\\nPlease review:\\n1. Code quality and patterns in the scene structure\\n2. Consistency across the modified scene files\\n3. Potential issues with the parallax implementation (scroll_scale values, layer ordering, naming)\\n4. Any typos (e.g., \\\"BackgroudSky\\\" vs \\\"BackgroundSky\\\")\\n5. Resource management and duplication concerns (Gradient/GradientTexture2D sub_resources are duplicated across scenes)\\n6. The new level.tscn file and its purpose\\n7. The tutorial scene changes\\n\\nReport any issues you find with severity levels.\"}"}}]}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"g9hq68yEpEKFSXoMLVnJTk7NcU307fK7","content":"{\"taskId\":\"tmp.z52een4Sa1\",\"response\":\"I'll start by examining the commit and each of the modified files to provide a comprehensive review.\\n\\nLet me also check the full content of some files to understand the broader context.\\n\\nNow I have all the information needed for a comprehensive review. Let me compile the findings.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# Code Review: Commit 215cf7c \\\"Parallaxing halfway done\\\"\\n\\n## 📋 Executive Summary\\n\\nThis commit introduces parallax scrolling layers across multiple forest level scenes and the tutorial scene. While the feature adds visual depth, there are several issues ranging from critical typos to resource management concerns that should be addressed before merging.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 🔴 Critical Issues\\n\\n### C1. Typos in Node Names — `BackgroudSky`\\n**Severity: 🔴 Critical**\\n\\nThe node is named `BackgroudSky` (missing the 'n') in **all four** scene files:\\n- `levels/00_forest/01.tscn` (line 23)\\n- `levels/00_forest/02.tscn`\\n- `levels/00_forest/03.tscn`\\n- `levels/level.tscn`\\n\\nThis typo will propagate into any code that references this node by name (e.g., `get_node(\\\"BackgroudSky\\\")`), making debugging frustrating. **Fix: Rename to `BackgroundSky` everywhere.**\\n\\n### C2. Incomplete Parallax Layers in `02.tscn` and `03.tscn`\\n**Severity: 🔴 Critical**\\n\\nThe \\\"complete\\\" parallax template in `01.tscn` has **6 layers**:\\n1. BackgroudSky (0, 0)\\n2. OtherTreeFar (0.2, 1)\\n3. OtherTreeClose (0.3, 1)\\n4. BackgroundTreesFartherAway (0.4, 1)\\n5. BackgroundTreesClose (0.6, 1)\\n6. BackgroundProps (0.8, 1)\\n\\n**`02.tscn` is missing:** `OtherTreeFar` and `OtherTreeClose`\\n**`03.tscn` is missing:** `OtherTreeFar`, `OtherTreeClose`, and `BackgroundProps`\\n\\nThis creates visual inconsistency across levels. The developer who wrote \\\"Parallaxing **halfway** done\\\" in the commit message is acknowledging this, but the inconsistency should still be resolved.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 🟠 High-Severity Issues\\n\\n### H1. Duplicated Gradient/GradientTexture2D Resources\\n**Severity: 🟠 High**\\n\\nThe exact same `Gradient` resource (identical colors) is duplicated as a `sub_resource` in **4 separate scene files**:\\n\\n| File | Gradient ID | GradientTexture2D ID |\\n|------|------------|---------------------|\\n| `01.tscn` | `Gradient_vhcel` | `GradientTexture2D_5gso3` |\\n| `02.tscn` | `Gradient_vhcel` | `GradientTexture2D_epyyu` |\\n| `03.tscn` | `Gradient_vv2jw` | `GradientTexture2D_r7adf` |\\n| `level.tscn` | `Gradient_vhcel` | `GradientTexture2D_hjsbj` |\\n\\nAll use: `colors = PackedColorArray(0.52156866, 0.7372549, 0.7058824, 1, 0.2784314, 0.4509804, 0.52156866, 0)`\\n\\n**Recommendation:** Extract this to a shared `.tres` file at `res://general/resources/fog_gradient.tres` and reference it via `ext_resource`. This reduces file bloat and ensures consistent fog appearance.\\n\\n### H2. Inconsistent Modulate Values for `BackgroundTreesClose`\\n**Severity: 🟠 High**\\n\\nThe `BackgroundTreesClose` layer has different modulate colors across files:\\n\\n| File | Modulate Color |\\n|------|---------------|\\n| `01.tscn` | `Color(0.18945992, 0.18572605, 0.25666898, 1)` |\\n| `02.tscn` | `Color(0.2, 0.19607843, 0.27058825, 1)` |\\n| `03.tscn` | `Color(0.2, 0.19607843, 0.27058825, 1)` |\\n\\nThis will cause visual inconsistency. If the color difference is intentional for artistic reasons, it should be documented. Otherwise, unify the values.\\n\\n### H3. Inconsistent Fog `scale` Values\\n**Severity: 🟠 High**\\n\\nThe Fog Sprite2D has different Y-scale values:\\n\\n| File | Fog position | Fog scale |\\n|------|-------------|-----------|\\n| `01.tscn` | `(608, 104)` | `(5, 1.375)` |\\n| `02.tscn` | `(608, 188)` | `(5, 0.71875)` |\\n| `03.tscn` | `(608, 64.000015)` | `(5, 1.6875)` |\\n| `level.tscn` | `(608, 104)` | `(5, 1.375)` |\\n\\nThese seem to be manually tuned per-level. While this may be intentional, the lack of a shared Fog resource makes it hard to maintain consistency. Consider a shared Fog node template.\\n\\n### H4. Removed `target_area_name` Fields\\n**Severity: 🟠 High**\\n\\nThe following `target_area_name` fields were removed:\\n- `01.tscn`: `target_area_name = \\\"LevelTransition\\\"` was removed from `LevelTransition`\\n- `02.tscn`: `target_area_name = \\\"LevelTransition\\\"` was removed from `LevelTransition`, `LevelTransition2`, and `LevelTransition3`\\n\\nIf the `LevelTransition` script relies on `target_area_name` for area-based targeting or debugging, this could cause broken transitions. Verify whether this is intentional.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 🟡 Medium-Severity Issues\\n\\n### M1. Generic Node Naming for Parallax TileMapLayers\\n**Severity: 🟡 Medium**\\n\\nInside the `Parallax2D` nodes, the child `TileMapLayer` nodes are generically named:\\n- `TileMapLayer` (used in BackgroudSky, OtherTreeFar, OtherTreeClose, BackgroundTreesFartherAway, BackgroundTreesClose)\\n- `TileMapParallax` (used in BackgroundProps)\\n\\n**Recommendation:** Use descriptive names like:\\n- `SkyTileMap`\\n- `TreeFarTileMap`\\n- `TreeCloseTileMap`\\n- `TreesFartherAwayTileMap`\\n- `TreesCloseTileMap`\\n- `PropsTileMap`\\n\\nThis improves scene readability and makes node references in scripts more robust.\\n\\n### M2. Inconsistent `scroll_offset` Usage\\n**Severity: 🟡 Medium**\\n\\n- `02.tscn`: `scroll_offset = Vector2(0, 48)` on both `BackgroundTreesFartherAway` and `BackgroundTreesClose`\\n- `03.tscn`: `scroll_offset = Vector2(-8, -24)` on `BackgroundTreesFartherAway` and `Vector2(0, -32)` on `BackgroundTreesClose`\\n- `01.tscn`: No `scroll_offset` set (defaults to 0)\\n\\nThe varying offsets suggest manual tuning. Document the reasoning or consider a shared pattern resource.\\n\\n### M3. `collision_enabled = false` Inconsistency\\n**Severity: 🟡 Medium**\\n\\n`BackgroundProps` has `collision_enabled = false` explicitly set, but the other parallax TileMapLayers do not have this property. If these layers are intentionally non-collidable, the flag should be set consistently across all of them (or the default should be verified).\\n\\n### M4. `LevelBounds` Height Changed\\n**Severity: 🟡 Medium**\\n\\n`LevelBounds.height` changed from `430` to `398` in `01.tscn` and `level.tscn`. Verify this is intentional and doesn't break camera bounds or level transition logic.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 🟢 Low-Severity Issues\\n\\n### L1. Purpose of `level.tscn` is Unclear\\n**Severity: 🟢 Low**\\n\\nThe new `levels/level.tscn` file appears to be a **template/prototype** level. It contains:\\n- Parallax layers and Fog\\n- `LevelBounds` with the new dimensions\\n- No `Player` node\\n- No `LevelTransition` node\\n- Empty `TileMapProps`, `TileMap`, and `TileMapAuto` nodes\\n\\n**Recommendation:** If this is a template, consider:\\n- Adding a comment at the top of the file explaining its purpose\\n- Renaming to `level_template.tscn` or moving to a `templates/` directory\\n- Adding a `README` note about it\\n\\n### L2. Generic TutorialNode Name\\n**Severity: 🟢 Low**\\n\\nThe new tutorial node in `tutorial.tscn` is named `TutorialNode`, which is the same as the script class name (`TutorialNode.tscn`). This is confusing in the scene tree.\\n\\n**Recommendation:** Rename to something descriptive like `VariableJumpHeight` or `JumpHeightTip`.\\n\\n### L3. Inconsistent Tutorial Text Delimiters\\n**Severity: 🟢 Low**\\n\\n- `TutorialNode`: `tutorial_text = \\\"Release jump to get a variable jump height <tab>\\\"`\\n- `OneWaySeeThem`: `tutorial_text = \\\"Go to the right to see some of the one way platforms. <space>\\\"`\\n\\nThe action is `[\\\"jump\\\"]` but the text says `<space>`. While `<space>` is visually clear, the action is `jump` which might be bound to multiple keys. Consider using `<jump>` consistently if that's the action name.\\n\\n### L4. `TileMapPattern` in Tileset\\n**Severity: 🟢 Low**\\n\\nA `TileMapPattern` sub_resource was added to `forgotten_forest.tres` and assigned to `pattern_0`. This is a Godot 4.3+ feature for tilemap patterns. The purpose and usage of this pattern is unclear from the diff.\\n\\n**Recommendation:** Add a comment explaining the pattern's purpose.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 📊 Summary Table\\n\\n| Severity | Count | Issues |\\n|----------|-------|--------|\\n| 🔴 Critical | 2 | C1 (Typo), C2 (Incomplete layers) |\\n| 🟠 High | 4 | H1 (Duplicated resources), H2 (Modulate inconsistency), H3 (Fog scale), H4 (Removed fields) |\\n| 🟡 Medium | 4 | M1 (Generic names), M2 (scroll_offset), M3 (collision_enabled), M4 (LevelBounds) |\\n| 🟢 Low | 4 | L1 (Template purpose), L2 (TutorialNode name), L3 (Tutorial text), L4 (TileMapPattern) |\\n| **Total** | **14** | |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ✅ Positive Observations\\n\\n1. **Scroll scale progression is logical**: The parallax layers follow a sensible depth progression (0 → 0.2 → 0.3 → 0.4 → 0.6 → 0.8).\\n2. **Node ordering is correct**: Parallax layers are ordered from farthest (Sky) to closest (Props), which is the correct rendering order.\\n3. **Tutorial changes are incremental**: The new tutorial node and text modifications are small, focused changes that improve the player experience.\\n4. **Level transitions in `02.tscn`**: Adding multiple level transitions (including upward `location = 2` and downward `location = 3`) shows thoughtful level design.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 🛠️ Recommended Priority Order\\n\\n1. **Fix the `BackgroudSky` typo** (C1) — affects all 4 files\\n2. **Extract shared Gradient resource** (H1) — reduces duplication\\n3. **Complete parallax layers in `02.tscn` and `03.tscn`** (C2) — ensure visual consistency\\n4. **Unify modulate colors** (H2) — fix visual inconsistency\\n5. **Verify `target_area_name` removal** (H4) — ensure no broken transitions\\n6. **Address remaining medium/low issues** as time permits\"}"}
{"role":"assistant","content":"","reasoning_content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"O6w8ywuEGElecoVW2a19csKLYWcykDK4","type":"function","function":{"name":"task","arguments":"{\"description\":\"Review Godot scene file structure\",\"agent\":\"subreviewer\",\"prompt\":\"Review commit 215cf7c (hash: 215cf7ca6a3a3f67cffec858bec8fcff7ff15b0f) titled \\\"Parallaxing halfway done\\\". This is a Godot game project.\\n\\nFocus on:\\n1. Godot-specific best practices - Are the scene structures following Godot conventions?\\n2. Parallax2D usage - Are the scroll_scale values appropriate for the intended effect? Is the layer ordering correct (closest to farthest or vice versa)?\\n3. Node naming - Check for consistency and any typos (e.g., \\\"BackgroudSky\\\" instead of \\\"BackgroundSky\\\", \\\"TileMapParallax\\\" as a node name that contains a TileMapLayer child)\\n4. Resource duplication - Each scene file creates its own Gradient and GradientTexture2D sub_resources for the fog effect. Is this efficient or should a shared resource be used?\\n5. The new level.tscn file - Is it properly structured? Does it make sense as a standalone file?\\n6. Tutorial scene changes - Are the tutorial node additions consistent with existing patterns?\\n7. Collision settings - Are collision_enabled=false set appropriately?\\n\\nReport any issues with severity levels.\"}"}}]}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"O6w8ywuEGElecoVW2a19csKLYWcykDK4","content":"{\"taskId\":\"tmp.sUJY0fPb7U\",\"response\":\"Now I have a complete picture of the commit. Let me compile my review:\\n\\n---\\n\\n# Code Review: Commit 215cf7c — \\\"Parallaxing halfway done\\\"\\n\\n## 1. Node Naming — Typos and Inconsistencies\\n\\n### 🔴 HIGH: Typo \\\"BackgroudSky\\\"\\nThe node is named **`BackgroudSky`** (missing the second \\\"g\\\") in all four scene files:\\n- `levels/00_forest/01.tscn`\\n- `levels/00_forest/02.tscn`\\n- `levels/00_forest/03.tscn`\\n- `levels/level.tscn`\\n\\nThis typo will propagate if any script references this node by name (e.g., `$BackgroudSky`). It should be **`BackgroundSky`**.\\n\\n### 🟡 MEDIUM: Generic/misleading child node names inside Parallax2D\\n\\n| Scene | Parent Node | Child Node Name | Issue |\\n|-------|-------------|-----------------|-------|\\n| 01.tscn | `BackgroudSky` | `TileMapLayer` | Generic name; doesn't describe content |\\n| 01.tscn | `OtherTreeFar` | `TileMapLayer` | Generic name |\\n| 01.tscn | `OtherTreeClose` | `TileMapLayer` | Generic name |\\n| 01.tscn | `BackgroundProps` | `TileMapParallax` | Name contains \\\"TileMap\\\" but IS a TileMapLayer — redundant/confusing |\\n| 02.tscn | `BackgroundProps` | `TileMapParallax` | Same issue |\\n| 03.tscn | `BackgroundProps` | `TileMapParallax` | Same issue |\\n\\n**Suggestion:** Name children descriptively, e.g., `SkyTilemap`, `FarTreesTilemap`, `CloseTreesTilemap`, `PropsTilemap`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Resource Duplication — Fog Gradient\\n\\n### 🟡 MEDIUM: Duplicated Gradient / GradientTexture2D sub_resources\\n\\nEach of the four scene files creates **its own copy** of the same fog gradient:\\n\\n| Scene | Gradient ID | GradientTexture2D ID |\\n|-------|-------------|---------------------|\\n| 01.tscn | `Gradient_vhcel` | `GradientTexture2D_5gso3` |\\n| 02.tscn | `Gradient_vhcel` | `GradientTexture2D_epyyu` |\\n| 03.tscn | `Gradient_vv2jw` | `GradientTexture2D_r7adf` |\\n| level.tscn | `Gradient_vhcel` | `GradientTexture2D_hjsbj` |\\n\\nAll four share identical `colors = PackedColorArray(0.52156866, 0.7372549, 0.7058824, 1, 0.2784314, 0.4509804, 0.52156866, 0)`.\\n\\n**Recommendation:** Create a shared resource file (e.g., `res://levels/resources/fog_gradient.tres` containing the Gradient and GradientTexture2D) and reference it via `[ext_resource]` in each scene. This reduces file size, ensures consistency, and makes future color tweaks a single edit.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Parallax2D Usage and scroll_scale Values\\n\\n### 🟢 LOW: scroll_scale values are reasonable\\n\\nThe parallax layers follow a logical progression from farthest to closest:\\n\\n| Layer Name | scroll_scale | Intended Distance |\\n|------------|-------------|-------------------|\\n| BackgroudSky | `Vector2(0, 0)` | Background / static |\\n| OtherTreeFar | `Vector2(0.2, 1)` | Far |\\n| OtherTreeClose | `Vector2(0.3, 1)` | Mid-far |\\n| BackgroundTreesFartherAway | `Vector2(0.4, 1)` | Mid |\\n| BackgroundTreesClose | `Vector2(0.6, 1)` | Mid-near |\\n| BackgroundProps | `Vector2(0.8, 1)` | Near |\\n\\nThe ordering is **correct** (closest layers have higher scroll_scale values, meaning they move more with the camera). The y-component of `1` means the layers scroll vertically at the same rate as the camera (no vertical parallax), which is appropriate for a side-scrolling game.\\n\\n### 🟢 LOW: Parallax2D structure\\n\\nEach `Parallax2D` contains a single `TileMapLayer` child. This is a valid pattern in Godot — `Parallax2D` is designed to contain multiple parallax layers. Using one `TileMapLayer` per `Parallax2D` node is fine for clarity, though if only one layer exists per parallax group, one could consider whether the `Parallax2D` wrapper is necessary. Given the project's structure, this is acceptable.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. Collision Settings\\n\\n### 🟢 LOW: `collision_enabled = false` is appropriate\\n\\nThe `collision_enabled = false` setting is applied to:\\n- `TileMapProps` in 01.tscn, 02.tscn, 03.tscn\\n- `TileMapParallax` (inside `BackgroundProps`) in 01.tscn, 02.tscn, 03.tscn\\n\\nThis is correct — these TileMapLayers contain decorative/parallax elements that should not produce collision. The actual collision tilemaps (`TileMap` and `TileMapAuto`) are separate and should have collision enabled (which they do by default).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. New level.tscn File\\n\\n### 🟡 MEDIUM: Missing LevelTransition node\\n\\nThe new `levels/level.tscn` is structurally sound (has `LevelBounds`, parallax layers, tilemaps), but it is **missing a `LevelTransition` node** that all other forest levels have. This means the player would have no way to exit this level.\\n\\n### 🟡 MEDIUM: Generic tilemap names\\n\\n| Node Name | Issue |\\n|-----------|-------|\\n| `TileMap` | Too generic; should be `TileMapCollision` or `TileMapMain` |\\n| `TileMapAuto` | Should be `TileMapAutotile` for clarity |\\n\\nCompare with `01.tscn` which uses `TileMapBackground` and `TileMapProps`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Tutorial Scene Changes\\n\\n### 🟢 LOW: New \\\"VariableJump\\\" tutorial node is consistent\\n\\nThe new `TutorialNode` under `TutorialManager` follows the exact same pattern as existing tutorial nodes:\\n```ini\\n[node name=\\\"TutorialNode\\\" parent=\\\"TutorialManager\\\" ... instance=ExtResource(\\\"5_cui05\\\")]\\nvisible = false\\noffset_right = 97.0\\noffset_bottom = 40.0\\ntutorial_text = \\\"Release jump to get a variable jump height <tab>\\\"\\nactions_to_press = Array[String]([\\\"continue\\\"])\\n```\\n\\n### 🟡 MEDIUM: \\\"OneWaySeeThem\\\" tutorial changes are logical but worth noting\\n\\n| Before | After | Assessment |\\n|--------|-------|------------|\\n| `tutorial_text = \\\"... <tab>\\\"` | `tutorial_text = \\\"... <space>\\\"` | ✅ Better — tells player what to press |\\n| `actions_to_press = [\\\"continue\\\"]` | `actions_to_press = [\\\"jump\\\"]` | ✅ Correct — matches the action being taught |\\n| `offset_bottom = 40.0` | *(removed)* | ⚠️ Minor inconsistency — all other nodes have explicit `offset_bottom = 40.0`. The value will fall back to the default, but explicit is better for readability. |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Removed `target_area_name` from LevelTransition nodes\\n\\n### 🟡 MEDIUM: Inconsistent removal of `target_area_name`\\n\\nIn `01.tscn` and `02.tscn`, the `target_area_name` property was removed from several `LevelTransition` nodes:\\n\\n**01.tscn:**\\n- `LevelTransition.target_area_name` — **removed** (was `\\\"LevelTransition\\\"`)\\n\\n**02.tscn:**\\n- `LevelTransition.target_area_name` — **removed**\\n- `LevelTransition2.target_area_name` — **removed**\\n- `LevelTransition3.target_area_name` — **removed**\\n- `LevelTransition4.target_area_name` — **kept** as `\\\"LevelTransition2\\\"`\\n\\nThe `level_transition.gd` script has a default value:\\n```gdscript\\n@export var target_area_name: String = \\\"LevelTransition\\\"\\n```\\n\\nSo removing it from the scene file means it uses the default. This is **functionally correct** but creates inconsistency — `LevelTransition4` in `02.tscn` explicitly sets a different area name while others rely on the default. If all transitions target the same area name, this is fine; if not, the removed entries should be explicitly set to avoid confusion.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Godot Scene Structure Conventions\\n\\n### 🟢 LOW: Scene structure follows Godot conventions\\n\\n- Root node is `Node2D` — correct for level scenes\\n- `[ext_resource]` and `[sub_resource]` sections are properly formatted\\n- `unique_id` values are used consistently\\n- `metadata/_custom_type_script` is set on `LevelBounds` nodes\\n- `z_index = 256` on `LevelBounds` for proper draw ordering\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Summary Table\\n\\n| Issue | Severity | Files Affected |\\n|-------|----------|----------------|\\n| `BackgroudSky` typo | 🔴 HIGH | 01.tscn, 02.tscn, 03.tscn, level.tscn |\\n| Duplicated fog Gradient resources | 🟡 MEDIUM | 01.tscn, 02.tscn, 03.tscn, level.tscn |\\n| Generic child node names (`TileMapLayer`, `TileMapParallax`) | 🟡 MEDIUM | 01.tscn, 02.tscn, 03.tscn |\\n| level.tscn missing LevelTransition | 🟡 MEDIUM | level.tscn |\\n| Generic tilemap names in level.tscn | 🟡 MEDIUM | level.tscn |\\n| Inconsistent `target_area_name` removal | 🟡 MEDIUM | 01.tscn, 02.tscn |\\n| `OneWaySeeThem` missing explicit `offset_bottom` | 🟢 LOW | tutorial.tscn |\\n| Parallax scroll_scale values | 🟢 LOW | 01.tscn, 02.tscn, 03.tscn |\\n| Collision settings | 🟢 LOW | 01.tscn, 02.tscn, 03.tscn |\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Priority fixes:**\\n1. **Rename `BackgroudSky` → `BackgroundSky`** across all scenes (high risk if any script references it)\\n2. **Extract fog Gradient to a shared resource** to reduce duplication and simplify future edits\\n3. **Add a `LevelTransition` node to `level.tscn`** if this level is intended to be playable/exitable\"}"}
